1|0@PS4^1439245997#ctyhlbh:Esham$:Not surprised this would work. I pc gamed for years and cleaned my pc case out every 6 months, the same period that i would format my entire PC and start fresh. At the end of the day the heat sensors tell the fans how fast to spin, if the fans are caked in dust they push less air and do not reduce the heat. Unit gets hot, fans spin, not enough air, spin faster. More dust &gt; faster fans &gt; more noise. Compound that with lack of airflow and it becomes apparent why a lot of people have loud fan problems and bricked systems. The best part is Sony KNOWS this failure rate and they KNOW people will do shit to prevent it. Its part of their forcasted sales i bet. 
